; DOMAIN: mathematics/number-theory/zeta-functions [CLOSED, derived 2026-08-01]; Claim: Zeta functions are meromorphic functions encoding arithmetic and geometric data. Key concepts: Riemann zeta function zeta(s) = sum 1/n^s with analytic continuation and functional equation; Euler product over primes connecting additive and multiplicative structure; Dedekind zeta function zeta_K(s) for number fields with class number formula relating residue at s=1 to class number, regulator, discriminant; Dirichlet L-functions L(s,chi) with Euler products and non-vanishing on Re(s)=1 proving Dirichlet's theorem on primes in arithmetic progressions; automorphic L-functions L(s,pi) attached to automorphic representations; Selberg zeta function for Riemann surfaces; the Riemann hypothesis about zeros of zeta(s) lying on Re(s)=1/2; explicit formulae connecting zero distribution to prime counting. Bridges to automorphic_forms (automorphic L-functions), analytic_number_theory (prime distribution, PNT), class_field_theory (Dedekind zeta, class number formula), and motives (motivic L-functions).;; Riemann zeta function: sum of n^{-s} for Re(s)>1, meromorphic continuation to C with simple pole at s=1
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Function $zeta) (--> ComplexVariable $s) (--> Equals (Apply $zeta $s) (SumOver $n (Power $n (Negate $s)))) (--> MeromorphicContinuation $zeta) (--> SimplePole $zeta 1))) (--> RiemannZeta $zeta)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Euler product: zeta(s) = product over primes of (1 - p^{-s})^{-1} for Re(s)>1, connecting additive and multiplicative structure
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Function $zeta) (--> ComplexVariable $s) (--> GreaterThan (RealPart $s) 1) (--> Equals (Apply $zeta $s) (ProductOver $p (Power (Subtract 1 (Power $p (Negate $s))) (Negate 1))) (--> Prime $p)))) (--> EulerProduct $zeta $s)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Functional equation: zeta(s) relates to zeta(1-s) via gamma factor and power of pi, symmetry about Re(s)=1/2
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Function $zeta) (--> ComplexVariable $s) (--> Equals (Apply $zeta $s) (Multiply (GammaFactor $s) (Power 2 $s) (Power (Pi) (Subtract $s 0.5)) (Apply $zeta (Subtract 1 $s)))))) (--> FunctionalEquation $zeta)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Dedekind zeta function: zeta_K(s) for number field K, sum over ideals of N(I)^{-s}, residue at s=1 gives class number formula
(|- ((==> (&& (--> NumberField $K) (--> Function $zeta_K) (--> ComplexVariable $s) (--> Equals (Apply $zeta_K $s) (SumOver $I (Power (Norm $I) (Negate $s)))) (--> MeromorphicContinuation $zeta_K))) (--> DedekindZeta $K $zeta_K)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Dirichlet L-function: L(s,chi) = sum chi(n)/n^s for Dirichlet character chi, Euler product over primes, non-vanishing on Re(s)=1
(|- ((==> (&& (--> DirichletCharacter $chi) (--> Function $L) (--> ComplexVariable $s) (--> Equals (Apply $L $s) (SumOver $n (Multiply (Apply $chi $n) (Power $n (Negate $s))))) (--> EulerProduct $L $s) (--> NonVanishing (Line (RealPart $s) 1)))) (--> DirichletLFunction $chi $L)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Automorphic L-function: L(s,pi) attached to automorphic representation pi, Euler product over local factors, analytic continuation and functional equation
(|- ((==> (&& (--> AutomorphicRepresentation $pi) (--> Function $L) (--> ComplexVariable $s) (--> Equals (Apply $L $s) (ProductOver $p (LocalFactor $L $p $pi))) (--> AnalyticContinuation $L) (--> FunctionalEquation $L))) (--> AutomorphicLFunction $pi $L)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Riemann hypothesis: all non-trivial zeros of zeta(s) lie on critical line Re(s)=1/2
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Function $zeta) (--> ComplexVariable $s) (--> NonTrivialZero $z $zeta) (--> Equals (RealPart $z) 0.5))) (--> RiemannHypothesis $zeta)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
